## What it is

An online survival game about gathering resources, building shelter, and managing encounters with other players.

## Is this your kind of game?

Rust is worth exploring if the ongoing decisions of multiplayer survival interest you. Think about whether you want an unpredictable environment shaped by other players, rather than a tightly scripted campaign.

## Download and purchase

This is a paid game. Check the official store for current regional pricing, editions, and purchase terms. Use the official Steam button on this page to open the publisher's listing. Installation is handled by Steam; GameNews does not host installers or game files.

Read the official listing’s multiplayer and installation requirements. Check the server rules before committing to a particular community.

## What the Steam listing shows

Checked 23 November 2026. Steam lists Facepunch Studios as both developer and publisher, with a release date of 8 February 2018. Steam lists Rust as multiplayer only: online PvP, online co-op, and cross-platform multiplayer, with no single-player mode. Valve Anti-Cheat is enabled.

The minimum column asks for 64-bit Windows 11, an AMD Ryzen 5 1400 or Intel Core i5-6600, 12 GB of memory, an AMD Radeon RX 470, NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1060, or Intel Arc A580, DirectX 11, a broadband connection, and 45 GB of storage. Steam says an SSD is highly recommended, or load times will be longer than average. A PC still on Windows 10 does not meet that minimum.

Steam’s content notice mentions violence and nudity. It says nudity, blood, player-made signs, voice chat, and text chat can be turned off in the in-game options.

## Sources and editorial basis

Product information checked against the [official Steam listing](https://store.steampowered.com/app/252490/?l=english) on 16 October 2026 and rechecked on 23 November 2026. Selected with reference to [Steam's most-played chart](https://store.steampowered.com/charts/mostplayed/). This is a researched profile, not a hands-on review or a search-volume ranking. Live prices, player counts, and performance scores are intentionally not quoted.
